# Harikane et al. (2023), ApJ 959, 39 (arXiv:2303.11946v3), Table 4: number densities of broad-line AGN (CEERS + GLASS NIRSpec)
# Redshift: z~5 bin, z_ave = 4.912
# Magnitude definition: M_UV = total (AGN+host) UV magnitude from Nakajima et al. (2023), not decomposed -> M1500
# Phi convention: linear Phi in cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (Planck18, h=0.6766); 1-sigma errors (upper, lower), Poisson + cosmic variance
# Note: Phi_AGN = f_AGN x galaxy UV LF (Harikane et al. 2022 DPL); f_AGN = 0.04.
# Note: the paper gives 1.4^{+1.9}_{-1.4}e-4; the lower delta is set to 1.37e-4 so that Phi - sigma stays > 0.
# Note: the M_UV = -21.5 bin is a 2-sigma upper limit (< 1.2e-5) and is in Harikane2023_ulimit.
#
# M_UV  Phi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
-18.5 1.4e-4 1.9e-4 1.37e-4
